diff --git a/dm/games/0400C76024710000/README.md b/dm/games/0400C76024710000/README.md
index 8de601d..9f8682f 100644
--- a/dm/games/0400C76024710000/README.md
+++ b/dm/games/0400C76024710000/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,60 @@
 
 A Switch 2 game: update v196608, SDK 20.5.15 built for the Switch 2 (`Ounce`), NVN2. Capcom's RE Engine, with Havok and Wwise. Modules `main` and `sdk`; `subsdk0` and `subsdk1` (C / libc) are not loaded. It plays on the Mac: the title, a new game's intro (the ship, the tower and the lunar base; last run on chain `79939b004bb5`) and, with the save those runs left, walking through the station's first rooms (chain `d24f05cf9d78`). Tested on an M4 Pro (48 GB) only.
 
+## iOS stability candidate
+
+A submission can finish on the CPU feedback path after a Metal error while the
+guest is waiting for a shared-event signal the queue did not execute. The host
+now publishes only the completed fence prefix, after its CPU-side reports land.
+The synthetic regression leaves the GPU signal absent and verifies that an
+ordinary fault wakes the wait path without revoking access.
+
+On iOS, near Metal's recommended working-set size, the completed scratch
+arenas above the existing reuse pool are eligible for retirement sooner.
+In-flight arenas retain the original fence protection. Outside that pressure
+range, the residency worker can apply the removals of idle upload staging
+allocations. The submit thread still applies them synchronously under pressure.
+The estimate is refreshed during loading even when submissions keep arriving
+without a new frame. Physical memory use during long sessions on 8 GB devices
+remains unverified.
+
+Tessellation without a geometry stage now depends only on the expansion
+pipeline. A failure to build the geometry-count pipeline is logged separately
+and only prevents replay when the draw has that stage. Whether this is behind
+any missing geometry in PRAGMATA remains open.
+
+The shader library and game build are unchanged. The absolute memory minimum,
+the opening movie's address fault, skipped tessellated draws and the cost of
+live streaming are open. Compare the same route with `DM_MEMSTAT=memstat.tsv`
+for resident memory and `DM_NVN_WAITS=1` for CPU waits. Inspect the first failed
+command buffer and the first tessellation refusal in `Documents/log.txt` before
+changing texture or shader behaviour.
+
+## iOS frame-time candidate
+
+- The A19 Pro capture recorded 638–1,113 ms per dirty-page census with
+  72.9–74.8 GiB free and 40.62 GiB of backing files. The disk watchdog can
+  skip this count when the entire backing range would still leave the
+  warning margin. It resumes the count as soon as that bound no longer
+  holds. This removes the timed census work on that capture's disk budget;
+  its effect on presented frame times still needs a replay.
+
+- [Raw pool table updates at command-buffer seal](../../../docs/reference/shaders.md#raw-pool-table-words-that-predate-the-pools) reduce repeated table builds and residency commits during streaming. The shader library is shared with the stability build.
+- The A19 Pro capture with `DM_NVN_GPUPROF=every:15` and `DM_NVN_PASSDUMP=every:30` associates the slow compute encoders with the SDF queue. At frame 1785, the encoder after pass 56538 took 243.1 ms out of 273.0 ms from first GPU timestamp to last. The pass dump records `251426e9d44fd558` (128 groups with 32 threads each) between the game's `0x821` barriers. At frames 1755 and 1845, the encoders after passes 53348 and 63004 took 263.5 and 299.5 ms and include `a39d5e8748386dea`. These are encoder timings, which cover multiple dispatches. The same run reports cap hits for both shaders and for `8c48c7ffd257c63d`.
+- The translated libraries for all three use a read-modify-write on word 513 of the storage buffer bound at push offset `0x120` to inspect the shared counter, and also update it from the kernel. The capture does not show the counter's value at the failing exit checks. It reports a recovered GPU page fault at frame 1004, before the long SDF bursts; a causal link is unverified. The queue mismatch in [#2664](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/issues/2664) remains open.
+
+The iOS build uses 32 workgroups for only the direct
+128 × 1 × 1 dispatches of these three 32-lane workers, on shader chain
+`63853cc4c4e3`. `DM_PRAGMATA_SDF_GROUPS=128` restores the guest grid. Values
+16 and 64 are also accepted. The emitted functions
+use the lane or local invocation ID, claim tasks through storage atomics,
+and have no grid-position input or dispatch-dimension driver reads. Their
+queue logic and compiled code stay the same.
+Compare the same route with both group counts. Check the loop hits, the
+duration of the affected encoders, and the image, especially effects and
+geometry that read the queue results. Real-device output equivalence and
+any speedup remain open.
+
 ## What it needs
 
